# Product change log

## When

Any time you change **client-facing product behaviour** (new/changed HTTP
flows, app UX contracts, env vars for frontend integration, removed
assumptions), update [`docs/PRODUCT_CHANGELOG.md`](../../docs/PRODUCT_CHANGELOG.md).

Also add or update a **sendable delta** under [`client-handoff/`](../../client-handoff/)
(with previous vs new flow, request/response shapes). Update module
`app/*/handoff/CHANGELOG_*.md` and `CLIENT_HANDOFF.md` when the long-term
reference changes.

Read this log (and `docs/BUGFIX_LOG.md`) before telling users or agents that
“E2E passing” means manual app/dashboard flows are complete.

## What to write

Add a new entry at the **top** of the Entries section (newest first). Use the
template in the log file.

Required fields:

- Date and short title
- Status (`shipped` / `partial` / `planned`)
- Area (module or flow)
- Client impact (what frontend/mobile must do)
- API / env changes (routes, fields, settings)
- Commit SHA(s) after the commit lands
- Handoff links

## Do not

- Use this for pure bugfixes — use `docs/BUGFIX_LOG.md`
- Duplicate long architectural prose from `spec/CHANGES.md`
- Record secrets, invite tokens, or PII in the log
